# The ability Thespian's Stage keeps as its copy's exception (CR 707.9b) works on the next turn: on turn 3 the Stage becomes a
# copy of Bot1's Island, on turn 5 that Island-Stage uses the kept ability to become a copy of Bot1's Mountain. The newer copy
# effect overwrites the older one (CR 613.2a, 707.2; the ruling): it is a Mountain and no longer an Island at all.

[Bot1 Deck]
Thespian's Stage
Sol Ring
Island
Mountain
Forest x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Thespian's Stage.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Thespian's Stage.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Thespian's Stage.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Island; Ability: becomes)
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1.Subtypes = Island
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain; Ability: becomes)
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Sol Ring; Island; Mountain; Mountain
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#1.Subtypes = Mountain
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#1.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#2.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Tapped = false
